exports[`a caveat is a promise > says how much of the promise surface it actually reaches > unverifiable 1`] = `
[
  "docx → md — Markdown has no syntax for a font, a colour or a page, so nothing in the output could carry them. True by the shape of the target rather than by anything the engine does.",
  "docx → pdf — A claim that the output does not match what Word would have produced. Checking it needs Word.",
  "odt → md — Markdown has no syntax for a font, a colour or a page, so nothing in the output could carry them. True by the shape of the target rather than by anything the engine does.",
  "md → docx — The Markdown fixture contains no raw HTML block, so the second half of this sentence has nothing to act on. Adding one would make it checkable.",
  "md → pdf — A claim about which typography was used, against an unnamed other renderer. There is nothing to compare the output to.",
  "md → pdf — emphasis dropped — nothing in a .pdf records it",
  "md → rtf — RTF marks a quotation with an indent, which is indistinguishable from any other indented paragraph, so "quotes survived" cannot be read back out of the file.",
  "txt → pdf — Where a line broke is a fact about the drawn page. A PDF records the positions of text runs, not that one of them is a continuation of another, so this cannot be read back.",
  "pdf → txt — Both halves need a fixture Recast does not have: a multi-column PDF, and a scanned one. The scanned case is covered by a refusal in _pdfread.ts rather than by this pair.",
  "pdf → md — A statement of where the inference fails, not a promise about the output. There is nothing here to hold Recast to.",
  "xlsx → pdf — The fixture workbook is three columns wide, so nothing is clipped and this claim is never put to the test. A wide fixture would make the first half checkable.",
  "ods → pdf — The fixture workbook is three columns wide, so nothing is clipped and this claim is never put to the test. A wide fixture would make the first half checkable.",
  "pptx → md — "Everything visual" names no feature, so there is nothing specific to look for. The checkable half of it is the sentence above, which is already checked.",
  "odp → md — "Everything visual" names no feature, so there is nothing specific to look for. The checkable half of it is the sentence above, which is already checked.",
]
`;
